# Altium


> Altium provides PCB design and electronics development (ECAD) software, covering schematic capture, PCB layout, component sourcing, and cloud-based design collaboration. This file is a semantic guide to Altium's website: its products, capabilities, audiences, educational resources, documentation, and support, with guidance for choosing the right page for a user.


Use this guide to identify the Altium section that best fits a user's intent, and to choose where to send them next.


Each section may include:


- **Audience:** the users, roles, needs, or situations for which the section is most relevant.
- **Flow:** when to select this section, and where to route the user next.
- **Representative pages:** selected official pages that serve as entry points into the section.


Use product pages for current commercial offerings and packaging. Use capability and use-case pages to determine whether Altium supports a particular workflow. Use official documentation for technical product behavior. Use Altium Resources for educational content and subject-matter exploration. Use support and training for post-purchase assistance and enablement.


Legacy product names, including CircuitStudio, Altium Designer, and Altium 365, still appear in documentation, support material, and search behavior. When a user is evaluating current Altium offerings, route them from these legacy brands to the Develop or Agile offering that best matches their team size and requirements. When a user needs technical information about an existing installation, prioritize the relevant documentation or support content.


## Homepage


The global home page at altium.com. It answers the general question of who Altium is, what it does, and where to go next, and it surfaces the main paths: the product tiers (Develop, Agile, Octopart Discover), audience pivots (personas, industries), and customer proof.


Audience: anyone whose intent is not yet specific, including users who know only the Altium brand and want an overview.


Flow: select only when the user's intent is unclear or purely brand-level, for example they reference Altium with no role, problem, industry, or product signal. Whenever the user's role, problem, industry, or product intent is known, prefer the more specific section over the homepage. From here, route to the product pages for tier selection, to capabilities for problem-first evaluation, to persona or industry pages for audience-specific needs, or to customer success for proof.


