## PRODUCTS


Altium's product suite: a three-tier ladder that consumed and repositioned the legacy Altium Designer (ECAD tool) and Altium 365 (cloud platform) licensing models and brands. Develop serves individual engineers and small teams (up to 5 people); Agile Teams serves larger teams (more than 5 people) needing more collaboration depth and out-of-the-box enterprise integration; Agile Enterprise serves large organizations or buyers with advanced compliance and customization needs. Octopart Discover sits alongside the ladder as a separate component-search and supply-chain offering. These pages cover benefits, features, pricing, and the criteria for choosing the right tier. The legacy /altium-designer and /altium-365 pages remain to catch users searching by the underlying/old product names and route them to the appropriate tier.


Audience: users who are choosing a product or considering an upgrade, and existing customers evaluating a move between tiers.


### Altium Develop: /develop


Altium Develop is the entry tier of the three-tier product ladder that replaced the legacy Altium Designer and Altium 365 brands. It serves individual engineers and small teams of up to 5 people, bundling the ECAD tool (formerly Altium Designer) and the cloud platform (formerly Altium 365) into a single subscription. Agile Teams and Agile Enterprise are the paths beyond it when team size or compliance needs exceed its scope.


Audience: electrical engineers, PCB designers, individual contributors, and small teams of up to 5 people who have evaluated Altium's capabilities and are choosing a product. Develop fits solo work and small-team collaboration.


Flow: use this as the primary product destination for individual engineers and teams of up to five people. Route larger teams to Altium Agile Teams. Route organizations needing advanced compliance, security, or custom integration to Altium Agile Enterprise. For a user still evaluating a particular workflow, use the relevant capability or use-case page first. After product selection, use contact, training, documentation, or support as appropriate.


- [Altium Develop product page](https://www.altium.com/develop)
- [Upgrade to Altium Develop from Altium Designer page](https://www.altium.com/develop/move)


### Altium Agile Teams: /agile/teams


The mid tier of the three-tier product ladder. Agile Teams is the out-of-the-box product for larger teams (more than 5 people) needing expanded collaboration, administration, and out-of-the-box enterprise integrations (SSO, PLM connectors) beyond Develop's scope. It sits between Develop (up to 5) and Agile Enterprise (large organizations or advanced needs): buyers here have outgrown Develop but do not yet need bespoke enterprise configuration.


Audience: engineering managers running teams of more than 5 people, enterprise IT evaluating tool standardization at team scale, and procurement comparing cost across team-size brackets. They want out-of-the-box enterprise integration and team collaboration without a long custom engagement.


Flow: use this for teams larger than five people that need out-of-the-box enterprise integration and team collaboration. Route to Agile Enterprise when the team needs custom configuration or advanced compliance. Route to Develop for a team of five or fewer. For a user comparing against a competitor at team scale, use the relevant compare page first. After selection, use contact for a sales conversation, or customer success for proof at team scale.


- [Altium Agile Teams product page](https://www.altium.com/agile/teams)


### Altium Agile Enterprise: /agile/enterprise


The top tier of the three-tier product ladder. Agile Enterprise is the fully custom enterprise offering for the largest organizations, or for any team with advanced compliance, custom integration, dedicated support, or bespoke configuration needs that Agile Teams cannot address. It is sold through direct sales engagement rather than self-serve checkout, and the page qualifies intent, presents enterprise-grade signals (compliance, security, scale), and starts a sales conversation.


Audience: VP Engineering, CTO, enterprise IT, and procurement at large organizations, or any buyer with advanced compliance or customization requirements. These are high-value engagements with long timelines, often reached through industry or compliance evaluation rather than product search.


Flow: use this for large organizations, or any buyer needing advanced compliance, security, custom integration, or dedicated support. Route to contact to start a sales conversation. For supporting evidence, use customer success for enterprise proof, industry pages for regulated-industry fit, and the Trust FAQs for compliance posture. If the user's requirements do not ultimately require advanced compliance, custom integration, dedicated support, or bespoke configuration, reconsider Agile Teams or Develop based on team size and workflow needs.


- [Altium Agile Enterprise product page](https://www.altium.com/agile/enterprise)


### Octopart Discover: /octopart-discover


Octopart Discover is Altium's systems-based electronic component discovery tool, a separate product that sits alongside the Develop, Agile Teams, and Agile Enterprise design-suite ladder rather than within it. It reuses the Octopart parts database with AI-powered systems-level search, sourcing intelligence, supplier lifecycle data, and BOM-stage decision support. It serves the procurement and sourcing side of the electronics workflow rather than the design side.


Audience: procurement managers, supply-chain specialists, and engineers involved in component sourcing, looking for parts availability, pricing trends, lifecycle status, supplier alternatives, and BOM risk signals.


Flow: use this for a user focused on component sourcing, supply-chain intelligence, or BOM risk, rather than board design. Route to Develop when the same organization also needs the design suite (the engineers who do the design work). Route to contact for sales or sign-up.


- [Octopart Discover product page](https://www.altium.com/octopart-discover)
- [BOM Management capabilities page](https://www.altium.com/capabilities/supply-chain/bom-management)


